1. WHAT YOU MAY DO
   The licensor ("Author") grants you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
   revocable licence to:
   (a) read and study the source code;
   (b) build the software from source and run it for your own personal,
       non-commercial use on devices that you own or control;
   (c) modify your own copy for that same personal use;
   (d) send suggestions, bug reports and patches (as text or a pull request branch
       inside the Author's own repository) to the Author.
   Creating a fork or any other copy of the repository on a hosting platform or
   elsewhere is NOT allowed unless the Author has given you permission in writing
   BEFORE you create it (an answer in an issue or by e-mail is enough). A permitted
   fork exists only for the purpose and for the time stated in that permission, and
   must clearly state who the Author is and link to the original repository.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
   Without the Author's prior written permission you may not:
   (a) copy, fork, publish, upload, mirror or otherwise distribute the software, or
       any substantial part of it (in whole or in part, in source or binary form,
       modified or unmodified), anywhere — including private and public repositories,
       archives and file-sharing services — except with the permission described in 1(d);
   (b) publish or distribute derivative works, forks, ports, "rewrites", themes or
       packages that contain or are derived from the software or its substantial parts;
   (c) use the software or any part of it for commercial purposes: sell, rent,
       sublicense, bundle it with a paid product or service, or use it to provide
       a paid or advertising-supported service;
   (d) present the software or derivative works as your own (for example, publish it
       under your name, a school/university assignment, a portfolio or a competition
       entry), remove or alter copyright notices, the name "NameLess", logos, commit
       history, authorship information or this licence, or release anything under a
       confusingly similar name;
   (e) use the software, its source code or its documentation as material for
       building datasets or for training machine-learning models, or collect it in
       bulk with automated tools;
   (f) circumvent any technical measure that the software uses to protect users
       (for example, the pairing and permission checks of NameLess Orbit) in order
       to access other people's devices.

3. CONTRIBUTIONS
   If you send a contribution (code, translation, documentation), you grant the
   Author a perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable, royalty-free licence to use, modify,
   sublicense and distribute it as part of the project, and you confirm that you have
   the right to do so. You keep authorship of your contribution.

4. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
   The software uses third-party components (for example Qt, FFmpeg, Quickshell and
   bundled themes, fonts and wallpapers). They remain under their own licences,
   which are not changed by this one. Nothing here restricts rights that you
   have under those licences, and the restrictions above do not apply to them.

5. TERMINATION AND ENFORCEMENT
   Your rights end automatically if you breach this licence. On termination you must
   stop using the software and delete all copies you made outside the permitted
   personal use. The Author may demand removal of unauthorised copies (including by
